# BUILD_SUMMARY.md — Update Policy

**Do not update this document automatically.**

- Update `docs/BUILD_SUMMARY.md` **only when the user explicitly asks** to update it (e.g. "update the build summary", "add this to BUILD_SUMMARY", "refresh BUILD_SUMMARY").
- Do **not** update it when:
  - Making new commits
  - Completing other tasks (fixes, features, refactors)
  - Following the "review and update documentation" rule for other docs
- If a task would normally trigger documentation updates, update other relevant docs (e.g. ARCHITECTURE.md, USER_GUIDE.md) but **skip** BUILD_SUMMARY.md unless the user specifically requested it.

This keeps the build summary as an intentional, on-demand record rather than an auto-maintained file.
